  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ecosystem Defence: Detecting, Disrupting and Deplatforming Malign Actors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Information manipulators are outpacing and outsmarting civic watchdogs and media across Africa, exploiting preexisting societal tensions to capitalise on conspiracist and anti-democratic sentiment that asserts that climate resilience and public health measures, along with gender or sexual rights, are being
covertly foisted on Africa by neocolonial or decadent Western forces.The project seeks to address information manipulation and its impact on human rights defenders championing gender and sexual identity rights as well as climate activists working towards a green transition by mapping and the mis/disinformation ecosystems in target countries as well as enhancing the capacity of media practitioners, researchers and activists to respond to, report on and pursue punitive measures for mis/information in country contexts as well as transnationally. The geographical focus of the project will be determined during the inception phase but will target South Africa and potentially Zimbabwe, Namibia, Madagascar, Botswana and Lesotho.</narrative>
  </description>
